cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this code or its results, please cite the dissertation."
title: "pricing-dt: where a fitted domain model enters an offline RL pipeline"
abstract: >-
  Code, environments and evidence for an MSc dissertation on offline reinforcement
  learning for repeated pricing and inventory decisions. One fitted demand model is held
  fixed and moved between three channels, selecting actions, generating training data and
  setting a conditioning target, and the consequences of its error are measured on two
  exactly-solvable environments where every policy's true value is known.
